{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779202882,"nonce":"Bts//R7aYNtXQ/uOvZ8mjxXpOHI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCvBa6Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135","origin":"github"},"title":"Deployment 2026-05-19: Starlink-only operation + OTH survey test","message":"## Operators\n\n- Roland + Claude Code Agent (Claude Opus 4.7, 1M context)\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub + boat compute)\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (if survey phase is reached)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n- Field agents started as needed.\n\n## Scope today\n\nTwo-phase test. Each phase is a go/no-go gate for the next.\n\n1. **Starlink-only operation at close range.** WiFi disabled at the\n   operator station; boat continues to publish on both paths, but the\n   operator can only receive Starlink. Validates that the fixes landed\n   since 2026-05-01 (PR\n   [#134](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/134)\n   coprime keyframe stagger; [rolker/udp_bridge#16](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/pull/16)\n   throughput regression fix; [rolker/camp#51](https://github.com/rolker/camp/pull/51)\n   NavSource QoS workaround) actually deliver the expected Starlink\n   budget headroom in practice.\n2. **Over-horizon survey attempt.** Conditional on phase 1: take the\n   boat out of line of sight on Starlink-only and run a short test\n   survey. First time over-horizon survey has been attempted; play\n   the rest by ear from what we see.\n\n## Open task issues in scope\n\n- [#130](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130) —\n  Field validation: over-horizon Starlink-only operation\n  (this deployment is the validation run)\n- [#124](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124) —\n  Post-mission tracker for 2026-05-01; today's run generates data\n  that helps close remaining checkboxes (§1.3 path attribution under\n  Starlink-only, §8 comms-loss recovery)\n- [#131](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/131) —\n  gabby sysctl UDP receive-buffer tuning — landed as part of pre-flight\n  on this deployment (staged for \"next deployment\" per the issue body)\n- [#134](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/134) —\n  OAK keyframe stagger (merged; bench-verify cadence pre-launch)\n- [rolker/udp_bridge#13](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/pull/13) —\n  resend loop amplification fix (in flight; if merged before launch,\n  validate impact; if not, baseline without)\n- [rolker/ros2_network_monitor#22](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/pull/22) —\n  MikroTik wireless event metrics (in re-review; useful diagnostic\n  for OTH, not deploy-blocking)\n\n## Carry-forward items to keep in mind (from 2026-05-01)\n\n- **RC mode-switch at fringe range** — FCU still honors RC channel\n  even with `FS_THR_ENABLE=0`. Mitigation: power off the RC controller\n  or pin its mode switch to AUTO/GUIDED before any over-horizon\n  attempt.\n- **BT `SkipUnknownTaskType` catchall** masks `FollowPath` aborts —\n  a survey-line abort silently marks the line \"done\" and the boat\n  falls into hover. **No upstream fix yet** (no issue filed against\n  `unh_marine_autonomy`); be alert if the survey line hover-and-quits\n  mid-leg.\n- **Mooring ball / perception→costmap** — segmentation didn't put\n  the 2026-05-01 mooring ball into the costmap. If the survey route\n  passes the same area, plan to avoid manually.\n\n## Hardware / software config\n\n_(to fill in at start-of-day: branches deployed, RMW, SBG / M3 /\nsv_bridge status, anything non-main)_\n\n## Tides + weather\n\n_(to fill in at start-of-day after operator confirms — README\nconvention: ask the operator first before pulling NOAA. Tide heights\nin metres; tide times explicitly TZ-tagged.)_\n\n## Pre-launch verification (before any over-horizon attempt)\n\n- [ ] `make sync` on dev; field hosts pulled latest from gitcloud\n- [ ] Bench-verify #134 keyframe cadence on a dev OAK (parse\n      `is_keyframe` on `/bizzy/sensors/cameras/oak_*/image_raw/ffmpeg`,\n      confirm IDR phase drift)\n- [ ] Sustained Starlink UDP test from gabby (`iperf3 -u -t 600 -b 5M`)\n      to characterize burst-loss events the 2026-05-18 15 s windows missed\n- [ ] WiFi-disabled rehearsal at pier: kill WiFi at operator, observe\n      what `udp_bridge` does on the boat side\n- [ ] RC controller mitigation in place (powered off or mode-switch\n      pinned)\n- [ ] FCU failsafes verified: `FS_THR_ENABLE=0`, `FS_GCS_ENABLE=0`,\n      GUIDED stale-cmd_vel HOLD behavior confirmed\n\n## Logs\n\n_(populated during the session as files appear)_\n\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-19_dev_logs.md` — dev side\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-19_gabby_logs.md` — gabby (field, gitcloud)\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-19_salmon_logs.md` — salmon (field, gitcloud)\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-19_mercat_logs.md` — mercat (if QINSy in use)\n\nPer docs/logs/README.md convention. Field hosts log to their own\nfiles; this issue is **shared with field agents via git-bug for\nread-only reference** (one-way distribution this deployment).\n\n## Wrap-up checklist\n\n- [ ] Push field-host logs to gitcloud at end of session\n- [ ] Pull field logs to dev worktree branch (`make sync` + per-branch\n      pull)\n- [ ] Audit full deployment for carry-forward\n- [ ] Open follow-up task issues for genuine carry-forward\n- [ ] Update `docs/roadmap.md` with anything deferred\n- [ ] Merge wrap-up PR (closes this issue)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}